{"abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","